  "character": "Ski-in/ski-out family resort at 1,350m at the foot of Pic Blanc (3,330m \u2014 Michelin Green Guide 3-star panorama). Closest resort to Grenoble in the Grand Domaine (55km). 11 hamlets. Gateway to 250km Alpe d'Huez ski area.",
  "research_status": "properly_sourced",
  "description": "Oz 3300 is the ski-in/ski-out resort of Oz-en-Oisans, named after Pic Blanc (3,330m \u2014 classified 3-star panorama in the Michelin Green Guide). Part of the Alpe d'Huez Grand Domaine (250km). 11 hamlets make up the commune including Oz Village, Le Roberand, Le Bessey, Sardonne, L'Ile d'Oz, Le Boulangeard, Le Pontonnier, La Beurri\u00e8re, La Vo\u00fbte, Le Pr\u00e9 de l'Arche, and L'Enversin. Only 55km from Grenoble (1 hour drive) \u2014 the closest Grand Domaine access. The Alpette Plateau and Lower Lakes are accessible by cable car. Known for the Oz canyon \u2014 a top canyoning spot in Oisans. Family-friendly, ski-in/ski-out, timber and stone architecture. 19th-century church in Oz Village with square bell tower.",
